A||||9||87GT||Thumping when turning left||||1
Z||000000||87GT||11-10-1999||11:01 PM||||I Just bought new tires for my GT, they were Eagle GTII's.  While my car was there, I had it aligned and the tie rods replaced.  It handles ten times better than it did before, but I have a problem that still occurs.  When I take a sharp left,(Like at a intersection)I feel this very bad thumping, and the steering wheel shakes quite a bit.  It sounds as if a tire is flat but it isnt.  I dont know much about fiero mechanics, but i was just praying for the love of god, that somebody here could tell me what is going on.  It does not sound too good.  Thanks.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierospeeder||11-11-1999||12:47 AM||||could be the strut i heard they sometimes make noise ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||11-11-1999||12:55 AM||||this happened as soon as the tires where changed? did you check lugs? Wheel bearings?||||reg||1
Z||000003||87GT||11-11-1999||01:42 AM||||The struts have been replaced.  They are about 5 mths old.  This problem has occured before.  It doesnt seem to happen all the time.  I have checked the lugs, tires everything.  I dont know, its very strange.  When turning to the right sharply, its as smooth as silk.  ??||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dan||11-11-1999||10:57 AM|||| Thumping in the turns?Thats also a symptom of bad velocity joints.Maybe.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DJRice||11-11-1999||05:38 PM||||Probably not in a RWD, since the axles arent involved in turning....||||reg||1
Z||000006||Patrick||11-11-1999||09:03 PM||||<BR>I suggest you simply limit your navigating to right hand turns only...||||reg||12
Z||000007||Tim||11-11-1999||10:42 PM||||Take it back to the alignment shop and have them test drive the car.  They should have done this anyways.  Go with the mechanic to point out the problem.||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||11-12-1999||01:11 AM||||check the rack unit for play. you could have it loading up in one direction more than another. a bad/damaged internal bushing or one of the rubber mounting bushings could do odd things.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Carrolles||11-15-1999||08:00 AM||||Since you had the tie rods replaced is the turning radius the same for both right and left turns?<P>I had a 79 Mustang that had front end work done.  When the tie rod ends were replaced the mechanic got the adjustment way off.  It would turn considerably sharper to the right than to the left.  While turning the extra sharp radius I noticed all kinds of strange new noises due to tire scrub and rubbing.  I had the tie rods adjusted again and this evened out the turning radius and did away with the odd noises.||||reg||1
